<title>UK: LME continues to work with regulators on Sumitomo.</title>
<headline>LME continues to work with regulators on Sumitomo.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>London Metal Exchange (LME) chief executive David King said the LME continues to work with all the regulatory and government agencies concerned with the Sumitomo Corp affair.</p>
<p>A reporter asked King about the firm's announcement of increased losses on alleged maverick trading in copper.</p>
<p>King said the LME did not know how the losses were arrived at. Significant London trades were made with firms that did not belong to the exchange. &quot;The LME is continuing to work with the all the regulatory and government agencies,&quot; King said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7729</p>
